ird-party AA/Vals standard benches; Moonshot publishes only proprietary ones).\n  * Removed superseded models: `gemini-3-flash-preview`, `gemini-2.5-flash-lite` (note: one of the four xagent-labeled models — its rows leave the capability logistic on the next retrain; difficulty axis unaffected), and `claude-sonnet-4.6` (dominated by Sonnet 5 at equal price). `z-ai/glm-4.7` intentionally stays: 3x cheaper than glm-5.2 with higher livecodebench — an undominated point on the cost frontier.\n  * Registry coverage is now gpqa_diamond 13/13, livecodebench 12/13 (deepseek-v4-flash's self-reported Think Max LCB was dropped pending an independent run; glm-5.2's Vals LCB 69.5 filled in).\n  * Router configs (`auto`, `quality-pair`, `cheap-pair`) route across the refreshed candidates.\n\n## Also\n\n  * CI wheel verification now checks the bundled model-profile count against the source registry instead of a hardcoded number (#21)\n\nAssets 2\n\nLoading\n\n### Uh oh!\n\nThere was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\n\n## v0.2.4\n\nv0.2.4\n\nCompare\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfix(proxy): normalize socks:// to socks5:// in proxy env vars (#1674) · MoonshotAI/kimi-cli@e622577 · GitHub (https://github.com/MoonshotAI/kimi-cli/actions/runs/23833283640)\nciteturn41123search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: last week; MoonshotAI  2. kimi-cli ... Triggered via pull request April 1, 2026 05:19 ... For more information see: https://github.blog/changelog/2025-09-19-deprecation-of-node-20-on-github-actions-runners/ [Button: Show more] [Button: Show less]\n\nThis repository was archived by the owner on Sep 23, 2026. It is now read-only.\n\n  1. MoonshotAI\n  2. kimi-cli\n\n# fix(proxy): normalize socks:// to socks5:// in proxy env vars (#1674) #7544\n\n  * Sign in to view logs\n\n## Summary\n\n# fix(proxy): normalize socks:// to socks5:// in proxy env vars (#1674)\n\n## \n\nfix(proxy): normalize socks: